{"id":2099,"date":"2025-05-08T11:00:00","date_gmt":"2025-05-08T16:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/?post_type=news&#038;p=2099"},"modified":"2025-05-08T11:04:12","modified_gmt":"2025-05-08T16:04:12","slug":"tides-of-innsmouth-available-to-pre-order-now","status":"publish","type":"news","link":"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/tides-of-innsmouth-available-to-pre-order-now\/","title":{"rendered":"Tides of Innsmouth available to pre-order now!"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p><strong>The next in the series of Investigators Gamebooks from Aconyte Books is available to pre-order now. Prepare yourselves, Investigators, for the journey to Innsmouth\u2026<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>From Aconyte: <\/p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\"><div class=\"lazyblock-block-quote-Z22zuuQ wp-block-lazyblock-block-quote\"><blockquote class=\"text-sand-white text-left px-8 md:pl-16 py-16 space-y-4 max-w-xl mx-auto\">\n    <p><p>Innsmouth is awash with sightings of a mysterious sunken pirate junk near the treacherous Devil Reef. Those rumors are an irresistible lure, drawing the Investigators of Arkham to the fog-laden Massachusetts town. But the thrill of discovery quickly wanes when you are faced with hostile locals, a missing marine archaeologist, and a family curse with tendrils that haunt your waking days. Solve the riddles, overcome tests, and wish for luck as you navigate the rotten streets of the decrepit town and beyond to save the world as you know it. However\u2026 choose wisely, Investigator, for betrayal lurks around every corner and the path you choose might awaken horrors from beneath the sea to sink us all.<\/p><\/p>\n    <cite><\/cite>\n<\/blockquote><\/div><\/blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p><em>The Tides of Innsmouth<\/em> is the second in the series of Investigators Gamebooks, following <em><a href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/books\/the-darkness-over-arkham\/\">The Darkness Over Arkham<\/a><\/em>, published last year. Both titles are by renowned gamebook author Jonathan Green. If you haven&#8217;t played a gamebook before they are \u2013 as the name suggests \u2013 a book and a game in one, where you take on the role of one of Arkham&#8217;s many famed investigators, and the choices you make as you read \u2013 as well as your success in various tests of skills \u2013&nbsp;determines the course of the story. <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-medium\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FARKGB02-The-Tides-of-Innsmouth-hi-res_3D_03_paperback_spine-172x300.png&amp;attachment_id=2106\" alt=\"The Tides of Innsmouth - 3D paperback\" class=\"wp-image-2106\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>This time, you can take your pick of three Investigators appearing in gamebook form for the first time \u2013 the sailor Silas Marsh, the trawler Marion Tavares, the folklorist K\u014dhaku Narukami, or any other previously published Investigator. Each Investigators Gamebook in the series is fully compatible with those that come before and after it, so if you enjoyed playing <em>The Darkness Over Arkham<\/em> with Agnes Baker, Rex Murphy or Nathaniel Cho, or one of the three free DLC Investigators \u2013&nbsp;Stella Clark, Amanda Sharpe or Skid&#8217;s O&#8217;Toole \u2013 you can continue to play as them in <em>The Tides of Innsmouth<\/em>. <\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/image-converter?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcdn.svc.asmodee.net%2Fproduction-arkhamhorror%2Fuploads%2F2025%2F05%2FTides-of-Innsmouth-pre-order_body_01-1024x581.png&amp;attachment_id=2102\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-2102\"\/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Investigators Silas Marsh, Kohaku Narukami and Marion Tavares<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n<p>And if you do choose to play with the same Investigator across multiple adventures, <em>The Tides of Innsmouth <\/em>introduces an experience system, offering a few little bonuses (and a few extra challenges) based on your experiences so far. We&#8217;ll be taking a closer look at how experience works in the Investigators Gamebooks series next week. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><em>The Tides of Innsmouth<\/em> releases worldwide on June 3, in both print and ebook editions, and is available for pre-order now. You can <a href=\"https:\/\/books2read.com\/TidesofInnsmouth\">find a retailer near you here<\/a>. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":2100,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false},"key-tag":[34,17,54],"class_list":["post-2099","news","type-news","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","key-tag-aconyte","key-tag-books","key-tag-investigators-gamebooks"],"acf":[],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO Premium plugin v22.3 (Yoast SEO v22.9) - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Tides of Innsmouth available to pre-order now! | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"The next in the series of Investigators Gamebooks from Aconyte Books is available to pre-order now.\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/www.arkhamhorror.com\/news\/tides-of-innsmouth-available-to-pre-order-now\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Tides of Innsmouth available to pre-order now! | ArkhamHorror.com | The Official Arkham Horror Website News\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"The next in the series of Investigators Gamebooks from Aconyte Books is available to pre-order now. Learn more at arkhamh